 # Auth: Delegation Tokens, Space Credentials, and App Gating
+
+## Plan 019 foundation status (2026-10-15)
+
+This section supersedes earlier implementation-status claims below. The older
+sections retain their historical spec pin; they are not current deployment evidence.
+Stratos currently has delegation ingestion, credential issuance, optional app gating,
+and local cnf.jkt/DPoP credential reads. Standard transport migration is separate.
+
+The candidate adds proposed Stratos-Request-Proof and Stratos-Service-Assertion
+helpers and injected admission composition only. No production route enables them.
+Standard Spaces HTTP Message Signatures remain unchanged. Clients use ephemeral
+P-256 keys bound by validated cnf.kid, without a registered client DID. Services
+prove identity with a published issuer-controlled DID method and a separate
+assertion over the exact request-proof digest. No new key purpose is required.
+
+Credential, client, service, and authorization checks precede one replay-consumed
+proof identity. The assertion has no second jti. Shared state must be atomic and
+retained through expiry plus skew; after state loss there is no replay protection
+for consumed identities. An unused stolen delegation can still win issuance.
+Possession is not permission or human consent. The PDS remains trusted.
+
+Keep delegation audience authorityDid#atproto_space_host separate from standard
+credential presentation audience (repository owner or authority by operation) and
+extension audience (receiving Stratos authority DID). Do not require the extension
+on foreign PDS hosts. Production ingress, cnf.kid migration, shared Redis probing,
+mutation, independent reviews, and source-bound AiaB remain outstanding.
+
 
